    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28352" root="عدم" body-key="E">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَعْدُومٌ</span></b>  [<i>Lacking, wanting, not found, not existing,</i> or <i>lost:</i> see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عُدِمَ</span>, of which it is the part. n.].
― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">يَكْسِبُ المَعْدُومَ</span> means <i>He is fortunate,</i> or
<i>possessed of good fortune;</i> [properly,] <i>he attains
what others are denied.</i> (K.) It is said in a
trad., <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">إِنَّكَ لَتَكْسِبُ المَعْدُومَ وَتُطْعِمُ المَأْدُومَ</span>. (M
and TA in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ادم</span>: expl. voce <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَدِيمٌ</span>.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  See also
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَدِيمٌ</span>.

